      "type": "product_bridge",
      "basis": "Robbery (120) and Burglary (220) offences -- the Incident Profile characterising the Crossover Heist -- correspond to the CLASSES of digital evidence collected in the case investigation (emails, files, URLs, disk images, registry keys, exhibits). This is a CLASS-level correspondence between the deployed Offence (NIBRS) and CaseObject (CASE) entities: those offence KINDS correspond to those evidence KINDS -- state it directly. It is not a per-record join: the products share no per-record key, so it never pairs a specific offence with a specific exhibit and no single figure spans both.",
